A||||2||Fformula88||87 Headlight motor questions||||5||
Z||000000||Fformula88||03-21-2000||08:06 PM||||My dads 87 Fiero is having trouble pushing up the Left headlight.  It goes up, but a lot slower than the right.  We lubricated the transmission and attachment points, but it hasn't helped any.  I was wondering if there is anything else I can do before shelling out the $130 for a new motor.  Thanx.<BR>||||reg||5
Z||000001||Robert||03-21-2000||08:58 PM||||You might want to check out this site first.<BR> <A HREF="http://www.execpc.com/~rodney1/87-88headlight.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.execpc.com/~rodney1/87-88headlight.htm</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||theogre||03-22-2000||07:57 PM||||to elaborate on what Robert said....<P>you need to pull the motor and split the gear case open. inside the case are 3 plastic pins. If they are broken the light may still come up, but slow. You'll need to order Rodney's pin kit to fix it. You may as well do both sides.<P>If the pins are not broken the motor itself may need cleaning and bearings greased. DO NOT oil or grease the armature or brushes. ||||reg||1
